// Module-level `let` zero-literal initializer audit (r2c module-let channel): the
// extractor records ONLY the aliased initializer syntax kind for a numeric literal
// (TS reverse-maps SyntaxKind.NumericLiteral to "FirstLiteralToken") and NEVER the
// literal text, so `= 0` is not derivable from the facts. Every key here was audited
// by reading the source: `<file>::<name>` declares a module-scope `let <name>:
// number = 0;` — the cheng zero-decl (`var <slot>: int64`) IS the JS initial value,
// the exact admission argument the NullKeyword/FalseKeyword kinds already carry. A
// key NOT in this set keeps the loud unresolved-identifier failure — never a guessed
// zero (a non-zero literal initializer would fabricate semantics; it also has no
// zero-decl representation and would need its own emission contract). Same
// hand-audited, not-a-generic-analyzer contract as CHT_DEFAULT_PARAM_VALUES above.
